# Cursor Rules for WorkoutGen

## Project Context
This is an Android Kotlin app using Jetpack Compose, Hilt, Room, and Clean Architecture.

## Code Style
- Use Kotlin idioms (scope functions, null safety, data classes)
- Use StateFlow for ViewModel state, Flow for repository data
- Use Material 3 components from androidx.compose.material3
- Add @Preview functions for composables
- Use suspend for one-shot operations, Flow for streams

## Architecture
- UI Layer: Compose screens + ViewModels
- Domain Layer: Use cases + Models + Repository interfaces
- Data Layer: Room entities + DAOs + Repository implementations

## Key Files
- AI Logic: domain/usecase/AIWorkoutGenerator.kt
- Models: domain/model/Models.kt
- Exercises: data/local/ExerciseLibrary.kt (870+ exercises)
- Programs: data/local/BuiltInPrograms.kt

## Patterns
- ViewModels: @HiltViewModel with StateFlow<UiState>
- Screens: @Composable with Scaffold, TopAppBar
- Navigation: type-safe routes in Navigation.kt

## Don't
- Use LiveData (use StateFlow)
- Use XML layouts (Compose only)
- Access Room from ViewModels directly (use repositories)
- Create singletons manually (use Hilt)

## Testing
- Unit tests for use cases and calculators
- Integration tests for repositories
- Compose tests for screens
